{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L104","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":104,"end":104}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":104,"end":104},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:2ebf623fa9b3120df645685845ec45cbf709464cf935c11c5d5eaca86dcaacf5","meta":{"text":"The outcome of an attempt, structured. `errorFingerprint` deduplicates repeat failures."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L115","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":115,"end":115}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":115,"end":115},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:a689c1e7c6504dbe54a158b5c56badd3e7bc76dc04f705f7f9670c714a29dd4d","meta":{"text":"A single immutable, content-addressed claim."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L136","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":136,"end":141}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":136,"end":141},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:06cd969901e13d5d146e448deef246adb71a3d05f03a47d1c64dbec0e48ca755","meta":{"text":"Untrusted staging for a proposed record (PRD: \"MemoryCandidate: untrusted staging representation\").\nTrust is implicitly `candidate` — a candidate NEVER enters normal recall. Promotion runs the\nadmissibility gate and, if it passes, creates a {@link MemoryRecord} (content-addressed; an\nidentical claim collapses to the same `mem:` id → dedupe)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L162","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":162,"end":166}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":162,"end":166},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:519d16054b5baf3a19c72f97c2b6576983eb773230db386821acaa54fc93bb10","meta":{"text":"A structured attempt-lifecycle event (PRD W5; the type lands in the schema). NEVER raw prompts,\ntranscripts, or chain-of-thought — only structured summaries, file/target refs, error\nfingerprints, and receipt ids."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L184","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":184,"end":188}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":184,"end":188},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:90ac4784b6deab182ba30f7e9fe339d5c75024b96234281aac6ab0fda01edd4c","meta":{"text":"A sanitized validation receipt (PRD §2 GateReceipt). NEVER persists raw stdout/stderr — only the\n`outputDigest` (blake3) and `assertions` (allowlisted named results). Produced ONLY by the CLI\nand CI runner (`runner: 'cli' | 'ci'`); the MCP server never executes (PRD)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L216","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":216,"end":216}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":216,"end":216},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:1ffcce9ec5a614215cb5ac6017f3e11530ed1bfe24751b1ccd07ab4a5a091d5d","meta":{"text":"A lifecycle decision event applied to a record (PRD §2 MemoryDecision). Immutable + append-only."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L232","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":232,"end":232}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":232,"end":232},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:6421285525a326b92596c4e073f2fb3153b290681301788224eef97c45e8bc43","meta":{"text":"A local feedback signal on a record (PRD §2 MemoryFeedback)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L248","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":248,"end":248}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":248,"end":248},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:2ca4e8de1241466b04bc89bbf23238f6741c963be5521152696cb9e2ae9da0c0","meta":{"text":"Which store a manifest describes (mirrors the three stores from PRD §2 storage layout)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L251","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":251,"end":251}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":251,"end":251},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:3ded3fd2c46f86ecd61b95835085995ae914fbd401d2c1da3d643f2138d8de63","meta":{"text":"Per-collection counts (mirrors the soul manifest's `stats` shape)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L261","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":261,"end":264}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":261,"end":264},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:724a3f48e60dfd249f014c685ff1478e163177cb5a5771e30ca93b969ef1f40d","meta":{"text":"The memory manifest (one per store: local repo, global, team). Mirrors the soul `Manifest` shape\n(format + schema version + repo + counts + lastUpdated) but for `memory-1`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L275","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":275,"end":275}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":275,"end":275},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:2a365c3ebeddf77c7dafb241124e7411949073eda29e3a9b6d739585ae3c6a67","meta":{"text":"Any memory-1 record line (a JSONL shard line is one of these)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L33","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":33,"end":33}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":33,"end":33},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:8f78bee05b3cc42822a4770ff8b2e524a701e5b0f82145087fee7f85673553c7","meta":{"text":"The boundary a claim is admitted within. `repo`-scoped claims carry the registry `repoId`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L42","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":42,"end":43}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":42,"end":43},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:5a52e6c42880a5fa055b5323864f49f0fc12470d626dbcca073d1a77c6bce5aa","meta":{"text":"Who authored the claim. An agent authored it; a human attested it. An agent assertion alone is\nnever evidence (PRD), but authorship records provenance regardless."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L51","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":51,"end":59}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":51,"end":59},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:69319a20c4c732f84aab1412e51d2c070545778814d0a408ebbd5d5d25a83d32","meta":{"text":"One admissibility-checked evidence item. Discriminated by `kind`; per-kind fields are optional.\nEach item carries its OWN `verdict` (PRD: \"every claim is checked independently\") — the record's\nEvidence verdict is the aggregate (valid ⟺ all valid; invalid if any invalid; degraded otherwise).\n`source-quote` reuses the grounding.ts quote-overlap-as-substring check (PRD §2 admissibility):\n`quote` must be a normalized substring of the rehydrated `soulId` anchor span, and `targetHash`\nmust match the live node hash (else degraded/orphaned at revalidation)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/types.ts@L94","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":94,"end":94}},"file":"packages/memory/src/types.ts","span":{"start":94,"end":94},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:8773566542ff990820d668dd75ac8e9d22e47339dceaa74a565a718c9e5b6639","meta":{"text":"A structured summary — the ONLY prose an attempt carries. Never raw prompts/transcripts/CoT (PRD)."}}
